# Product-molecularity fixture: one complex A.B.C. The rule deletes A-B and
# claims three products, A, B and C, leaving C untouched. The only C is the one
# bonded to B, which a bimolecular rule may match only with
# block_same_complex_binding=False; C stays bonded to B, so the products do not
# separate and the rule must not fire (Afree stays 0). Main fired it (Afree 1).
begin model
begin parameters
  k 1
end parameters
begin molecule types
  A(b)
  B(a,c)
  C(b,x)
end molecule types
begin seed species
  A(b!1).B(a!1,c!2).C(b!2,x) 1
end seed species
begin observables
  Molecules Afree A(b)
end observables
begin reaction rules
  A(b!1).B(a!1) + C(x) -> A(b) + B(a) + C(x) k
end reaction rules
end model
writeXML()
